**Related Spec**: specs/470-fix-sdlc-execute-closing-worker-panes-while-their-background-work-runs/

# File: hooks/register.test.ts, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute-supervisor.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-finalize-verification.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-prompt-snippets.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/491-make-the-sdlc-execute-session-an-opus-supervisor-that-inspects-and-steers-every-worker-stage/requirements.md
Feature: The /sdlc-execute session supervises every worker stage on Opus

  @SCN001
  Scenario: An Opus or Fable session runs execute on its own model
    Given a Herdr Claude Code session whose model is "claude-opus-5-5" or "claude-fable-5-1"
    When the person runs /sdlc-execute #42
    Then the execute workflow is submitted
    And main-loop requests keep the session model
    And workers start with start, implement and deliver on haiku, verify on opus, and repair on opus

  @SCN002
  Scenario: A lesser model is told to switch and stopped
    Given a session whose model is "claude-sonnet-5-5"
    When the person runs /sdlc-execute #42
    Then the command prints "/sdlc-execute requires an Opus session (current: claude-sonnet-5-5). Switch with /model opus and run /sdlc-execute again."
    And it exits non-zero without rendering or submitting the workflow

  @SCN003
  Scenario: An unreadable session model fails closed
    Given the host throws when the session model is read
    When the person runs /sdlc-execute
    Then the command prints the refusal with "current: unknown" and exits non-zero without rendering

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Control returns at every stage boundary with a stage report
    Given a supervised execute run on issue 42
    When the verify worker writes its handoff
    Then a stage report is yielded before the worker pane closes
    And it names the issue, stage, worker, pane, handoff, HEAD before and after, commits, out-of-spec paths, gate status and failure history
    And it carries the readiness status, reason code, gaps, and the report's critical and remaining issues

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Accept continues with the existing routing
    Given a stage report for a passed implement handoff
    When the supervisor accepts it
    Then the implement pane closes and verify is dispatched next

  @SCN006
  Scenario: The supervisor prompts the live worker
    Given a stage report whose worker pane is open
    When the supervisor sends guidance
    Then the guidance reaches that worker's pane
    And a new stage report follows the same worker's fresh handoff

  @SCN007
  Scenario: The supervisor re-dispatches with guidance
    Given a stage report for a failed implement handoff
    When the supervisor re-dispatches with guidance "use the existing parser"
    Then the pane closes and a new implement worker starts with that guidance and the failure evidence in its instructions

  @SCN008
  Scenario: Verify is re-run after an environmental failure
    Given a failed verify stage report at source HEAD H
    When the supervisor re-dispatches verify with guidance
    Then a new verify worker starts at H with no implement repair first
    And deliver is dispatched only after the full registered gate passes

  @SCN009
  Scenario: The supervisor halts the run
    Given a stage report
    When the supervisor halts with diagnosis "host disk full"
    Then the run exits non-zero with "supervisor_halt: host disk full"
    And owned panes close, the lease is released, and the branch is unchanged

  @SCN010
  Scenario: Supervision cannot bypass the full-green gate
    Given a verify stage whose registered gate is not full-green
    When the supervisor accepts the report or re-dispatches deliver
    Then deliver is not dispatched

  @SCN011
  Scenario: The supervisor checks in on a running worker
    Given a worker still running after the check-in interval
    When the interval passes or its pane output stays unchanged for the interval
    Then a check-in report is yielded while the worker keeps running
    And it names the worker, pane, time since dispatch, pane tail and last change, waiting marker, commits, out-of-spec paths and failure history

  @SCN012
  Scenario: A check-in can continue, steer, re-dispatch or halt
    Given a check-in report
    When the supervisor answers continue, prompt, redispatch or halt
    Then waiting resumes, guidance reaches the running worker, the stage restarts with guidance, or the run halts

  @SCN013
  Scenario: Guidance to a busy worker is queued
    Given a worker in the middle of a tool call
    When the supervisor prompts it at a check-in
    Then the prompt is accepted without a delivery wait
    And the controller keeps waiting for that worker's handoff without a deadline

  @SCN014
  Scenario: The issue-scope marker always matches the resolver
    Given a passing verification report whose hand-written marker lists scenario titles
    When the report is finalized
    Then the report's marker equals the resolver marker and the verify handoff passes

  @SCN015
  Scenario: Workers never move the shared checkout's branch
    Given the rendered prompt for any execute worker stage
    Then it forbids switching the checkout's branch to read another ref
    And it names git show, git diff and git worktree as the alternatives

  @SCN016
  Scenario: Supervisor tests ignore an ancestor module package type
    Given a "type": "module" package.json above the execute supervisor fixture
    When the supervisor fixture runs execute
    Then its helper scripts run as commonjs and the run reaches its blocking worker command

  @SCN017
  Scenario: A failed integration probe names a real cause
    Given herdr integration status returns no result, a spawn error, a signal, or a non-zero exit
    When /sdlc-execute stops with "Run: herdr integration install claude"
    Then stderr names the cause or "probe returned no result" and never "exit undefined"
